<h2>3. Authentication via Google (OAuth 2.0)</h2>
<p><strong>This sign-in method is not enabled in the current version of MyClash.</strong> This section describes it in advance, and takes effect on the day it is switched on. Until then, use email and password or a sign-in link.</p>
<p>MyClash offers sign-in via your Google account, provided by Google LLC (Google OAuth 2.0).</p>

<h3>3.1 Data retrieved from Google</h3>
<p>When signing in via Google, MyClash accesses only the following information, with your explicit consent:</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Google email address</td><td>Unique identifier for your MyClash account</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Display name</td><td>Pre-filling your profile</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Profile picture (avatar)</td><td>Display within the application (optional)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>We do not access any other Google data (contacts, calendar, Drive, Gmail, etc.).</p>

<h3>3.2 Google's terms</h3>
<p>Use of Google sign-in is also subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. MyClash is not affiliated with Google LLC.</p>

<h3>3.3 Revoking access</h3>
<p>You can revoke MyClash's access to your Google account at any time from your Google account security settings: <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Revoking access will sign you out of MyClash but will not delete your account or your data.</p>

